<title>GERMANY: Rhenag H1 profits fall while sales increase.</title>
<headline>Rhenag H1 profits fall while sales increase.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to end June</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   16.4    vs 20</p>
<p>    Gas sales				    178.2   vs 163.7</p>
<p>    Electricity sales			  16.5    vs 16.4</p>
<p>    Water sales				  2.2     vs 2.1</p>
<p>    No of employees (at end June)	  725     vs 741</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German energy group is Rheinische Energie AG (Rhenag), which is a subsidiary of mixed utility group RWE AG.</p>
<p>Rhenag said in a letter to shareholders that sales opportunities for natural gas were still good, even if the outlook for the building industry looked poor, and the group expected a satisfactory number of new customers in 1996.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
